                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.51/579: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-01T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 1, 1920—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>162. Embassy’s telegram dated May 22, 1920, 4 p.m. Banks in New York City which
                    carry accounts of National Railways, Comision Monetaria, and Financial Agent,
                    Government of Mexico, have notified the Department that they will not honor any
                    checks which may be drawn on said accounts until Government now functioning in
                    Mexico is recognized.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
